# Written by hand, in the format BioNetGen writes, with initial amounts given inline. BNG2.pl
# 2.9.3 would write each of these as a named _InitialConc parameter instead, but an older or
# hand-made network file can carry the expression itself. BNGL reads 10^R as a power (100 at
# R = 2) and 2^3 as 8. Python's eval read them as 10 XOR R and 2 XOR 3 = 1.
begin parameters
    1 R    2  # Constant
    2 k    0.1  # Constant
end parameters
begin species
    1 A() 10^R
    2 B() 2^3
end species
begin reactions
    1 1 0 k #_R1
end reactions
begin groups
    1 Atot                 1
    2 Btot                 2
end groups
